      "answer": "Oroville, California",
      "quote": "Concow, or Konkow, people are the northwestern or foothill branch of the Maidu people, who traditionally spoke the Concow language Mooretown Rancheria is headquartered in Oroville, California. The tribe is governed by a democratically elected, tribal council, and the current tribal chairperson is Ben Clark. The Mooretown Rancheria is a federally recognized ranchería with an area of 109 acres. It is located in the community of Oroville East, in suburban Oroville.",
